  "description": "Symbol -> cross-asset reference ETF and sector for the 71 EQUITY rows of the 100-name breadth universe (research/breadth/universe.json, 2019-01-30). Read by iap.features.reference_map under --xasset-reference symbol_map (feature identity xasset_v2); the v1 'first ETF row' rule (features/context.py) is unchanged and remains the default. ETF rows always reference themselves (as in v1); FX rows are untouched.",
  "rule": "reference_etf = QQQ when the name was a Nasdaq-100 constituent on the as_of date, SPY otherwise.",
  "source": "Nasdaq-100 membership as of the 2019-01-30 session as recalled from public index-provider reconstitution announcements (December 2017 and December 2018 annual reconstitutions and intra-year replacements), written by the REL-07 session on 2026-10-18 from public reference knowledge, NOT from a licensed constituent file. Sectors are copied from configs/reference/sectors.json (same as_of, same caveats).",
  "limitations": [
    "Membership is point-in-time as of 2019-01-30, NOT current membership; it is not valid for any other date.",
    "Not taken from the index provider's constituent file; names with confidence 'low' are uncertain and treated as non-members (SPY). The owner should replace this file with a vendor or index-provider constituent file before any registered study (REL-08).",
    "Foreign ADRs (VALE, ABEV, ITUB, BBD, PBR, GGB, NOK, BABA, JD, NIO, PDD) trade on a US clock but their home-market factor is not captured by SPY or QQQ.",
    "The two VIX ETNs (TVIX, VXXB) are classed EQUITY by the ingest and get SPY, which is a poor reference for a volatility product.",
    "One reference per name: no sector ETF is used as the reference even where one is in the universe (XLF, XLE, XLK, ...); a sector-relative variant would be a new map version.",
    "Every reference ETF named here must be an ETF row of the dataset's instruments.json; a missing reference fails closed at context build."
  ],
